{"id": "brilliant-facet-plan", "verdict": "rewrite", "score": 3, "styleFit": 4, "literal": false, "problems": ["The lattice renders as a generic 60 degree triangle grid, not the 45 and 22.5 degree steps of a brilliant facet plan, so the source idea is lost.", "The glint reads as a star cross sparkle with spokes, close to the sparkle icon cliche, rather than light caught inside facets.", "The lattice covers a broad corner wedge at even weight, so it feels like generic tech wallpaper more than one cut mark."], "fix": "Build the lattice from the real brilliant grammar: 8-fold radial divisions with kite, star and upper girdle facets at 45 and 22.5 degree steps, set off-centre and fading to nothing. Have the fire-blue light fill two or three facet planes with a soft gradient as it passes, with no star spokes, and keep the rest of the near-black field empty for type."}
