{"id": "wycinanki-layer-bloom", "verdict": "rewrite", "score": 2, "styleFit": 2, "literal": false, "problems": ["A thin red, black and green trim at the very top reads as a Christmas garland or party bunting, not as a crafted paper cut.", "The uniform scallops and teeth repeat like a clip-art border, with no visible mirror axis, no layered depth and no offset shadows at render size.", "The motion is invisible across the frames: the layers barely move, so the slow mirrored slide adds nothing.", "Pure red over pure green is the loudest pairing on the card; the cobalt and off-white restraint of real wycinanki is lost."], "fix": "Take the grammar of wycinanki rather than a trim strip: a central mirror axis, three stacked cut layers with crisp edges and a soft 1 to 2 px offset shadow, and folded-paper repeats that change in scale toward the centre so the symmetry is felt. Use the off-white ground with one cobalt or deep green layer and red only as a small focal cut near the axis, and let the layers drift a visible 4 to 8 px on a slow custom ease so the motion reads as paper settling."}
